{"step_index":1485,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:54:46Z","thinking":"**Exploring Roman Domination in Graphs**\n\nConsidering the case where the number of vertices, $n$, equals $2k$, the radius of the graph is less than or equal to $k$.  A key question is determining the minimum Roman domination number for a connected graph with *n* vertices. A star graph $K_{1, n-1}$ appears promising; the center node receives a label of 2, while leaves are labeled 0, resulting in a weight of 2. The radius of this star graph is 1, and the relationship holds: 1 + 1 ≤ 2. Further exploring a path graph $P_n$ reveals radius $\\lfloor n/2 \\rfloor$ and a weight of $\\lceil 2n/3 \\rceil$.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/.venv/bin/python3 -c \\\"\\nimport networkx as nx\\nimport scipy.optimize as opt\\nimport numpy as np\\n\\ndef rdn(G):\\n    n = G.number_of_nodes()\\n    nodes = list(G.nodes())\\n    node_idx = {nodes[i]: i for i in range(n)}\\n    c = np.array([1]*n + [2]*n)\\n    A_ub = []\\n    b_ub = []\\n    for i in range(n):\\n        row = [0]*(2*n)\\n        row[i] = 1\\n        row[n+i] = 1\\n        A_ub.append(row)\\n        b_ub.append(1)\\n    for v in nodes:\\n        i = node_idx[v]\\n        row = [0]*(2*n)\\n        row[i] = -1\\n        row[n+i] = -1\\n        for u in G.neighbors(v):\\n            row[n+node_idx[u]] = -1\\n        A_ub.append(row)\\n        b_ub.append(-1)\\n    integrality = [1]*(2*n)\\n    bounds = opt.Bounds([0]*(2*n), [1]*(2*n))\\n    res = opt.milp(c=c, integrality=integrality, bounds=bounds,\\n                   constraints=opt.LinearConstraint(A_ub, -np.inf, b_ub))\\n    return int(round(res.fun))\\n\\nmax_r_for_gamma = {}\\nfor n in range(2, 9):\\n    for G in nx.graph_atlas_g():\\n        if G.number_of_nodes() == n and nx.is_connected(G):\\n            r = nx.radius(G)\\n            g = rdn(G)\\n            if g not in max_r_for_gamma or r > max_r_for_gamma[g]:\\n                max_r_for_gamma[g] = r\\n\\nfor g in sorted(max_r_for_gamma):\\n    print(f'gamma_R = {g}: max radius = {max_r_for_gamma[g]}, max radius + 1 = {max_r_for_gamma[g] + 1}')\\n\\\"\"","Cwd":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9\"","RunPersistent":"false","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"10000","toolAction":"\"Testing max radius for each gamma_R in graph atlas\"","toolSummary":"\"Test max radius for gamma_R\""}}]}
