{"step_index":1523,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:56:01Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-12T01:56:01+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-12T01:56:01+02:00\nFile Path: `file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/antigravity/check.sh`\nTotal Lines: 51\nTotal Bytes: 2182\nShowing lines 1 to 51\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: #!/bin/bash\n2: # check.sh — the ONLY command an agent may run.\n3: #\n4: #   /abs/path/tools/antigravity/check.sh FILE.lean\n5: #\n6: # Lives outside every agent workspace and is hashed by guard.sh: agents can\n7: # write inside their workspace, so a checker kept there could be rewritten into\n8: # anything. It screens the file first (tools/antigravity_handoff.py lint), because\n9: # Lean elaboration can itself run shell commands; then elaborates it with bare\n10: # `lean` and an explicit LEAN_PATH, and prints every theorem's axioms. Nothing\n11: # here depends on $HOME — agents run under a private one — and `lake` is never\n12: # involved (in this project lake deletes Mathlib when it cannot re-clone).\n13: set -uo pipefail\n14: f=\"${1:?usage: check.sh FILE.lean}\"\n15: [ -f \"$f\" ] || { echo \"CHECK: no such file: $f\"; exit 2; }\n16: \n17: ROOT=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$(readlink -f \"$0\")\")/../..\" && pwd)\"\n18: # Tool paths come from a protected file, not from the home directory: agents run\n19: # under a private HOME, and on compute nodes `getent passwd` reports a different\n20: # home (/home/<user>@ad…) than the one the tools live in.\n21: ENVF=\"$ROOT/handoff/.agf_env\"\n22: export ELAN_HOME=\"$(grep -m1 '^AGF_ELAN_HOME=' \"$ENVF\" 2>/dev/null | cut -d= -f2-)\"\n23: LEAN=\"$ELAN_HOME/bin/lean\"\n24: [ -x \"$LEAN\" ] || { echo \"CHECK: lean not found (ELAN_HOME='$ELAN_HOME' from $ENVF)\"; exit 2; }\n25: PY=\"$ROOT/.venv/bin/python\"\n26: LP_FILE=\"$ROOT/handoff/.agf_lean_path\"\n27: [ -s \"$LP_FILE\" ] || { echo \"CHECK: missing $LP_FILE\"; exit 2; }\n28: export LEAN_PATH=\"$(cat \"$LP_FILE\")\"\n29: \n30: orig=\"$(ls \"$ROOT\"/benchmark/challenges_*/\"$(basename \"$f\")\" 2>/dev/null | head -1)\"\n31: if ! \"$PY\" \"$ROOT/tools/antigravity_handoff.py\" lint ${orig:+--original \"$orig\"} \"$f\"; then\n32:   echo \"CHECK: refused to elaborate — remove the construct named above.\"\n33:   exit 3\n34: fi\n35: \n36: tmp=\"$(mktemp --suffix=.lean)\"\n37: cp \"$f\" \"$tmp\"\n38: for t in $(grep -oE '^theorem +[A-Za-z0-9_]+' \"$f\" | awk '{print $2}'); do\n39:   echo \"#print axioms $t\" >> \"$tmp\"\n40: done\n41: timeout 1800 \"$LEAN\" \"$tmp\"\n42: rc=$?\n43: rm -f \"$tmp\"\n44: if [ $rc -eq 0 ]; then\n45:   echo \"CHECK: elaborated. Allowed axioms: propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound.\"\n46:   echo \"       'sorryAx' in a list above means that theorem is unfinished.\"\n47: else\n48:   echo \"CHECK: FAILED (exit $rc)\"\n49: fi\n50: exit $rc\n51: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
